    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59760" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραυγ-ή</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>crying, screaming, shouting</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς ἥδε κ.</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Telecl.
				35
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραυγὴν θεῖναι, στῆσαι</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1510
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1529
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					3.1.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραυγῇ χρῆσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. γίγνεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					13.71
				</span></i>
			; rarely of a <i>shout of joy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PPetr.
				3p.334
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				1.42
			</span></i>: in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				2.35
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραυγὴ Καλλιόπης</span>, as an
			instance of bad taste, cited from.<i><span class="en">
				Dionys.Eleg.
			</span></i>(<i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i>) by <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1405a33
			</span></i>.</div>
